messages:
Asha V: Noticing a weird UX flicker in the browser streaming SDK when the auth token rotates. Sometimes a 3-6 char tail from the previous chunk appears at the start of the resumed event.

Riley M: Is that happening on our EventSource polyfill or native EventSource? Which browsers?

Asha V: Polyfill + Chrome and Safari. Native ES doesn't reproduce (probably because it handles last-id header differently). Repro steps: start stream -> wait for short-lived token to expire -> SDK refreshes and reconnects -> resumed payload begins with a 4-char overlap of previous tail.

Jordan T: Likely parse buffer leaking across reconnect. Our polyfill keeps partial parse state to avoid dropping fragments; if the server resumes inclusive of the last byte, we get double-play. Node SDK clears parser on reconnect so it never sees this.

Asha V: snippet from the polyfill parse loop:
```
let buf = '';
polyfill.ondata = (chunk) => {
  buf += chunk;
  const parts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = parts.pop() || '';
  for (const p of parts) handleEventBlock(p);
};
// reconnect currently preserves buf
```

Riley M: Two easy options: (A) clear buf on reconnect (defensive), (B) change resume semantics server-side to be exclusive (server starts after last delivered byte). Ideally both.

ops-bot: FYI - we have nginx idle timeout 60s in staging which frequently closes mid-chunk in stress tests.

Jordan T: Also consider client-side dedupe by event sequence/offset. If we attach a monotonic seq to each chunk, client can ignore duplicates. That helps when resume semantics differ.

Asha V: Proposed quick fix: clear parse buffer on reconnect + add opt-in resumePreference: "exclusive"|"inclusive" in SDK. Default to exclusive to match Node behavior. I'll open a small PR that adds unit tests simulating a mid-chunk TCP close.

Riley M: Ops ask: add keepalive heartbeats (server sends ":hb\n\n" every 15-30s) to reduce proxy mid-chunk closes. Ensure heartbeats are ignored by renderer and excluded from usage metrics.

Jordan T: Agree. Spec work: unify resume header handling (Last-Event-ID header vs resume_token query param). Both SDKs should accept both forms for parity. Also implement a fallback if resume fails N times: switch to short polling to avoid repeated visual duplicates.

Asha V: I'll file an issue with a minimal repro script and attach traces. PR will include tests + a small e2e that forces a TCP termination mid-chunk.

ci-bot: started CI for branch fix/polyfill-buffer-clear (build 6062) :rocket:

Riley M: Action items:
- Asha: PR to clear buffer on reconnect, add resumePreference opt, unit + e2e tests
- Jordan: spec for header parity + client dedupe by seq
- Ops: example nginx config and keepalive recommendation

Asha V: thanks all — will tag you on the PR and close once green. :white_check_mark:
